msgid "Log in again after exiting the client"
msgstr "Log in again after exit"

msgid "When enabled, log in again after the desktop application exits and restarts. Minimizing or hiding the application does not count as exiting. Disabled by default."
msgstr "When enabled, log in again after the desktop application exits and restarts. Minimizing or hiding the application does not count as exiting. Disabled by default."

msgid "Client login idle timeout (minute)"
msgstr "Idle timeout (minutes)"

msgid "Log in again when the idle timeout is reached. 0 disables the limit (default). Real keyboard and mouse input in the main window, separate asset windows and built-in websites counts as activity. An open connection, background output and automatic refresh do not count. Input in external software such as Xshell or MSTSC, and in some cross-origin embedded pages, cannot be captured. Using only these areas, watching without input for a long time, or failed reports due to network issues may still trigger the idle timeout. Time is measured from the last activity confirmed by the server."
msgstr "Log in again when the idle timeout is reached. 0 disables the limit (default). Real keyboard and mouse input in the main window, separate asset windows and built-in websites counts as activity. An open connection, background output and automatic refresh do not count. Input in external software such as Xshell or MSTSC, and in some cross-origin embedded pages, cannot be captured. Using only these areas, watching without input for a long time, or failed reports due to network issues may still trigger the idle timeout. Time is measured from the last activity confirmed by the server."

msgid "Client login lifetime (minute)"
msgstr "Login lifetime (minutes)"

msgid "Measured from client login; activity and token refresh do not extend it. 0 disables the lifetime limit (default). Exit and idle timeout settings still apply. Log in again when the lifetime ends."
msgstr "Measured from client login; activity and token refresh do not extend it. 0 disables the lifetime limit (default). Exit and idle timeout settings still apply. Log in again when the lifetime ends."

